:math1-10","source_crop":{"x":332.3,"y":431.6,"width":242.4,"height":288.4},"visual_crop":null,"needs_visual":false,"question_lines":["A manager is responsible for ordering supplies for a shaved ice shop. The shop’s inventory starts with 4,500 paper cups, and the manager estimates that 70 of these paper cups are used each day. Based on this estimate, in how many days will the supply of paper cups reach 1,700?","A) $20$","B) $40$","C) $60$","D) $80$"],"visual_after_line":null},{"id":"practice-test-6:math1-11","source_crop":{"x":35.9,"y":109.1,"width":242.4,"height":425.5},"visual_crop":null,"needs_visual":false,"question_lines":["$$y>4x+8$$","For which of the following tables are all the values of $x$ and their corresponding values of $y$ solutions to the given inequality?","A)","x\ty","2\t19","4\t30","6\t41","B)","x\ty","2\t8","4\t16","6\t24","C)","x\ty","2\t13","4\t18","6\t23","D)","x\ty","2\t13","4\t21","6\t29"],"visual_after_line":null},{"id":"practice-test-6:math1-12","source_crop":{"x":35.9,"y":534.6,"width":242.4,"height":185.4},"visual_crop":null,"needs_visual":false,"question_lines":["Which expression is equivalent to $(x^2+11)^2+(x-5)(x+5)$?","A) $x^4+23x^2-14$","B) $x^4+23x^2+96$","C) $x^4+12x^2+121$","D) $x^4+x^2+146$"],"visual_after_line":null},{"id":"practice-test-6:math1-13","source_crop":{"x":314.3,"y":109.1,"width":242.4,"height":158.5},"visual_crop":null,"needs_visual":false,"question_lines":["The function $h$ is defined by $h(x)=\\frac{8}{5x+6}$. What is the value of $h(2)$?"],"visual_after_line":null},{"id":"practice-test-6:math1-14","source_crop":{"x":314.3,"y":267.7,"width":242.4,"height":452.3},"visual_crop":{"x":0.1,"y":0.03,"kind":"figure","width":0.82,"height":0.36},"needs_visual":true,"question_lines":["The figure shows the lengths, in inches, of two sides of a right triangle. What is the area of the triangle, in square inches?"],"visual_after_line":-1},{"id":"practice-test-6:math1-15","source_crop":{"x":53.9,"y":109.1,"width":242.4,"height":430.3},"visual_crop":{"x":0.06,"y":0.07,"kind":"figure","width":0.88,"height":0.43},"needs_visual":true,"question_lines":["The graph models the number of active projects a company was working on $x$ months after the end of November 2012, where $0\\le x\\le6$. According to the model, what is the predicted number of active projects the company was working on at the end of November 2012?","A) $0$","B) $5$","C) $8$","D) $9$"],"visual_after_line":-1},{"id":"practice-test-6:math1-16","source_crop":{"x":53.9,"y":539.4,"width":242.4,"height":180.6},"visual_crop":null,"needs_visual":false,"question_lines":["The relationship between two variables, $x$ and $y$, is linear. For every increase in the value of $x$ by 1, the value of $y$ increases by 8. When the value of $x$ is 2, the value of $y$ is 18. Which equation represents this relationship?","A) $y=2x+18$","B) $y=2x+8$","C) $y=8x+2$","D) $y=3x+26$"],"visual_after_line":null},{"id":"practice-test-6:math1-17","source_crop":{"x":332.3,"y":109.1,"width":242.4,"height":294.5},"visual_crop":null,"needs_visual":false,"question_lines":["$$P=N(19-C)$$","The given equation relates the positive numbers $P$, $N$, and $C$. Which equation correctly expresses $C$ in terms of $P$ and $N$?","A) $C=\\frac{19+P}{N}$","B) $C=\\frac{19-P}{N}$","C) $C=19+\\frac{P}{N}$","D) $C=19-\\frac{P}{N}$"],"visual_after_line":null},{"id":"practice-test-6:math1-18","source_crop":{"x":332.3,"y":403.7,"width":242.4,"height":316.3},"visual_crop":null,"needs_visual":false,"question_lines":["$$w^2+12w-40=0$$","Which of the following is a solution to the given equation?","A) $6-2\\sqrt{19}$","B) $2\\sqrt{19}$","C) $\\sqrt{19}$","D) $-6+2\\sqrt{19}$"],"visual_after_line":null},{"id":"practice-test-6:math1-19","source_crop":{"x":35.9,"y":109.1,"width":242.4,"height":323.8},"visual_crop":null,"needs_visual":false,"question_lines":["The table shown summarizes the number of employees at each of the 17 restaurants in a town.","Number of employees\tNumber of restaurants","2 to 7\t2","8 to 13\t4","14 to 19\t2","20 to 25\t7","26 to 31\t2","Which of the following could be the median number of employees for the restaurants in this town?","A) $2$","B) $9$","C) $15$","D) $21$"],"visual_after_line":null},{"id":"practice-test-6:math1-20","source_crop":{"x":35.9,"y":432.9,"width":242.4,"height":287.1},"visual_crop":null,"needs_visual":false,"question_lines":["What is the $y$-coordinate of the $y$-intercept of the graph of $\\frac{3x}{7}=-\\frac{5y}{9}+21$ in the $xy$-plane?"],"visual_after_line":null},{"id":"practice-test-6:math1-21","source_crop":{"x":314.3,"y":109.1,"width":242.4,"height":321.7},"visual_crop":{"x":0.05,"y":0.08,"kind":"figure","width":0.9,"height":0.58},"needs_visual":true,"question_lines":["The graph of $y=2x^2+bx+c$ is shown, where $b$ and $c$ are constants. What is the value of $bc$?"],"visual_after_line":-1},{"id":"practice-test-6:math1-22","source_crop":{"x":314.3,"y":430.8,"width":242.4,"height":289.2},"visual_crop":null,"needs_visual":false,"question_lines":["In 2008, Zinah earned 14% more than in 2007, and in 2009 Zinah earned 4% more than in 2008. If Zinah earned $y$ times as much in 2009 as in 2007, what is the value of $y$?","A) $0.5600$","B) $1.0056$","C) $1.1800$","D) $1.1856$"],"visual_after_line":null},{"id":"practice-test-6:math1-23","source_crop":{"x":53.9,"y":109.1,"width":242.4,"height":610.9},"visual_crop":{"x":0.08,"y":0.02,"kind":"figure","width":0.84,"height":0.24},"needs_visual":true,"question_lines":["Circle $A$ (shown) is defined by the equation $(x+2)^2+y^2=9$. Circle $B$ (not shown) is the result of shifting circle $A$ down 6 units and increasing the radius so that the radius of circle $B$ is 2 times the radius of circle $A$. Which equation defines circle $B$?","A) $(x+2)^2+(y+6)^2=(4)(9)$","B) $2(x+2)^2+2(y+6)^2=9$","C) $(x+2)^2+(y-6)^2=(4)(9)$","D) $2(x+2)^2+2(y-6)^2=9$"],"visual_after_line":-1},{"id":"practice-test-6:math1-24","source_crop":{"x":332.3,"y":109.1,"width":242.4,"height":610.9},"visual_crop":{"x":0.08,"y":0.02,"kind":"figure","width":0.84,"height":0.28},"needs_visual":true,"question_lines":["Right triangle $ABC$ is shown. What is the value of $\\tan A$?","A) $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{54}$","B) $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$","C) $\\sqrt{3}$","D) $27\\sqrt{3}$"],"visual_after_line":-1},{"id":"practice-test-6:math1-25","source_crop":{"x":35.9,"y":109.1,"width":242.4,"height":521.8},"visual_crop":null,"needs_visual":false,"question_lines":["At the time that an article was first featured on the home page of a news website, there were 40 comments on the article. An exponential model estimates that at the end of each hour after the article was first featured on the home page, the number of comments on the article had increased by 190% of the number of comments on the article at the end of the previous hour. Which of the following equations best represents this model, where $C$ is the estimated number of comments on the article $t$ hours after the article was first featured on the home page and $t\\le4$?","A) $C=40(1.19)^t$","B) $C=40(1.9)^t$","C) $C=40(19)^t$","D) $C=40(2.9)^t$"],"visual_after_line":null},{"id":"practice-test-6:math1-26","source_crop":{"x":314.3,"y":109.1,"width":242.4,"height":358},"visual_crop":null,"needs_visual":false,"question_lines":["x\tg(x)","-27\t3","-9\t0","21\t5","The table shows three values of $x$ and their corresponding values of $g(x)$, where $g(x)=\\frac{f(x)}{x+3}$ and $f$ is a linear function. What is the $y$-intercept of the graph of $y=f(x)$ in the $xy$-plane?","A) $(0,36)$","B) $(0,12)$","C) $(0,4)$","D) $(0,-9)$"],"visual_after_line":null},{"id":"practice-test-6:math1-27","source_crop":{"x":314.3,"y":467.2,"width":242.4,"height":163.7},"visual_crop":null,"needs_visual":false,"question_lines":["In right triangle $ABC$, angle $C$ is the right angle and $BC=162$. Point $D$ on side $AB$ is connected by a line segment with point $E$ on side $AC$ such that line segment $DE$ is parallel to side $BC$ and $CE=2AE$. What is the length of line segment $DE$?"],"visual_after_line":null}]
